# The kit is executed, not just read, and half of what it ships is
# extensionless (`gh-tok`, `run-hook-python`, `claude-wrapped`, `fleet-watch`).
# A checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` — the Git for Windows default,
# which a WSL user inherits whenever the repo lives on the Windows side —
# rewrites those to CRLF, and a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` script with a trailing \r
# fails at the shebang with a bare "no such file or directory" naming an
# interpreter that plainly exists.
#
# `text=auto` still runs git's binary detection, so this normalises source
# without touching anything that isn't; `eol=lf` pins the working-tree ending
# regardless of the platform default. Repo-wide rather than per-glob because
# the failure mode is one missed extensionless file, and there is nothing here
# that wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
